<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chorotega</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chorotega are an Indigenous people of the Pacific coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, living at the Spanish conquest in what are now western Nicaragua and the Nicoya peninsula of Costa Rica. Speakers of an Oto-Manguean language related to languages of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, they are thought to have migrated south around 800 CE. They grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and made fine polychrome pottery and carved stone metates.</p></div>
